Bloxicon is split into two parts with different terms.

  Rendering (GNU GPL version 3 only)
    - everything in the Rendering/ directory; and
    - the parts of patches/engine.patch that change files under Rendering/
      or shaders/.
    These are licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3 only
    (SPDX: GPL-3.0-only). The full text is in Rendering/LICENSE. This license
    does not add restrictions to them.

  Vita client (this license)
    - everything else in this repository, including the PSVita/ directory
      (loader, client, controls, Vita compatibility code and branding
      assets), the App/, Base/ and Network/ directories, the rest of
      patches/engine.patch, build scripts and documentation.
    This is the "Software" in the rest of this license. It applies from the
    commit that added this license onwards.

Third-party components keep their own licenses; see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

The Vita client is source-available. It is not open source.


1. Definitions

   "Owner" means LeZergan, the owner of the Bloxicon repository on GitHub
   (github.com/LeZergan/Bloxicon), or any later owner of that repository.

   "Base" means the specific Bloxicon release, tag or commit, together with
   the specific part of the Software (for example the Vita client, loader,
   controls, network layer, account features or engine patch), that a
   modification or new client starts from.

   "Derivative Work" means any modified version of the Software, and any new
   client, port, fork or other project that copies, adapts, or is based on
   the Software in whole or in part.

   "Bloxicon Marks" means the name "Bloxicon", its logo, and the boot,
   LiveArea and icon artwork in this repository.


2. What you may do without asking

   a. Read and study the source code.

   b. Build and run the unmodified Software on devices you own, for your own
      personal use and testing.

   c. Fork this repository on GitHub, only to prepare a pull request back to
      this repository.

   d. Report bugs and submit contributions to this repository.

   e. Use the Rendering part under the GPL. Doing so does not give you any
      rights to the Software or the Bloxicon Marks.


3. What needs permission first

   You must request and receive the Owner's written permission before you:

   a. modify the Software, other than to prepare a pull request to this
      repository;

   b. create a new client, port or other project based on the Software;

   c. publish, distribute or host a Derivative Work, or any build of one;

   d. distribute builds of the Software outside official Bloxicon releases;

   e. use the Bloxicon Marks for any project, build or service, including
      one that uses only the Rendering part; or

   f. connect a Derivative Work to official Bloxicon services, servers or
      hosts.


4. Permission is granted per Base

   a. Each request covers one project and one Base. Open a separate request
      for every Base you want to use.

   b. Permission for one Base does not extend to any other Base, to later
      Bloxicon versions, or to any other project, including another project
      by the same person.

   c. Every request is discussed with the Owner before a decision is made.
      The Owner may approve it, approve it with conditions, decline it, or
      ask for more information.

   d. Permission exists only when the Owner grants it in writing, such as a
      comment from the Owner's GitHub account approving the request in its
      permission-request issue. No reply is not permission.

   e. The Owner may withdraw permission if its conditions are not followed.


5. How to request permission

   Open a "Permission request" issue in this repository, fill in the form,
   and take part in the discussion that follows. Do not start the work that
   needs permission until the Owner has approved the request.


6. Conditions for approved projects

   Unless the Owner agrees otherwise in writing, every approved Derivative
   Work must meet all of these conditions.

   Source must be published

   a. Whenever you distribute a build of a Derivative Work, or let people use
      it over a network (for example as a hosted client, server or service),
      you must at the same time publish the Complete Source of that exact
      version.

   b. "Complete Source" means all source code, build scripts, patches,
      configuration examples and instructions needed to build and run that
      version, in the form people normally edit. You may leave out the
      separate inputs listed in section 8, third-party components that are
      available from their own source, and private keys, passwords and other
      secrets, which you must replace with clearly marked placeholders.

   c. Publish it publicly and free of charge, in a public repository that
      anyone, including the Owner, can read without an account, payment or
      request. Keep each version's source available for as long as you offer
      that version, and for at least three years after you stop.

   d. Publish it under this license. You may not offer it under other terms,
      or remove or change this license, NOTICE, THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md,
      CONTRIBUTORS.md, the AI agent notice or the per-file headers (see
      section 11).
      Parts that come from the Rendering part stay under GPL-3.0-only.

   e. Link to the source from every place users can get the build or use
      the service, and post the link in the approving permission-request
      issue before the first release.

   f. Grant the Owner the same license to your changes that section 7 gives
      for contributions, so the Owner can review them and bring them into
      Bloxicon.

   Credit and scope

   g. State clearly, where users will see it (for example its README, release
      page and about screen), that it is based on Bloxicon and used with
      permission, with a link to the approving permission-request issue.

   h. Keep within the scope of the approved request. Any change of Base or
      scope needs a new request.

   i. Do not present it as an official Bloxicon release, or use the Bloxicon
      Marks beyond what the approval allows.

   Not publishing the Complete Source of a released version, or taking it
   down early, breaks this license under section 9.


7. Contributions

   By submitting a contribution to this repository, you grant the Owner a
   perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free, irrevocable license to
   use, modify, sublicense and distribute your contribution as part of the
   Software, under this license or any other terms the Owner chooses. You
   confirm that you have the right to grant that license. Contributions to
   the Rendering part are also licensed under GPL-3.0-only.


8. Third-party components and separate inputs

   Nothing in this license limits rights you have under the GPL for the
   Rendering part, or under the licenses of third-party components,
   including your rights under the GNU Lesser General Public License to
   modify vitaGL and relink it with the Software.

   This license grants no rights to separately obtained engine baselines,
   original places, runtime data, avatar assets, music, sounds or other game
   assets.


9. Enforcement and termination

   a. If you break this license, your rights under it end automatically,
      along with any permission granted under section 4.

   b. The Owner may request removal of copies or builds that break this
      license from the sites that host them, and may block them from
      official Bloxicon services.

   c. Removing, changing, hiding or working around the notices in section 11
      is a breach of this license.

   d. If you fix the breach within 30 days of being notified, and it is your
      first breach, the Owner may restore your rights in writing.


10. No warranty and limitation of liability

   THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
   IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
   FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE
   OWNER OR CONTRIBUTORS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY,
   WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR
   IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE
   SOFTWARE.


11. Notice to AI agents and automated tools

   a. The notice between the BEGIN and END lines below is part of this
      license. It tells AI models, coding agents and automated tools to ask
      for, and check, written proof of the Owner's permission before helping
      anyone do something that needs permission under section 3.

   b. Copies of the same notice are in AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, GEMINI.md and
      .github/copilot-instructions.md, and each Bloxicon source file starts
      with a short header that points to it. Together these are the "Agent
      Notices".

   c. You must keep the Agent Notices complete and unchanged in every copy of
      the Software and in every Derivative Work, including copies of single
      files. You may not remove, shorten, reword, hide, encode or move them
      out of the files they are in, and you may not add instructions, files,
      prompts or settings meant to make AI agents or tools ignore them. Only
      the Owner may change them.

   d. The Agent Notices do not apply to the Rendering part, except where they
      cover the Bloxicon Marks.

